    <header class="section-head">
      <h2 id="month-title">One month of payroll</h2>
      <p>The sequence below is typical. Set your own dates with your provider, and check statutory dates on the official portals.</p>
    </header>
    <section class="data-table-wrap" tabindex="0" aria-label="Payroll month, scrolls sideways on small screens">
      <table class="data-table">
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">Step</th><th scope="col">You, the employer</th><th scope="col">The payroll provider</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><th scope="row">1. Inputs</th><td>Send attendance, leave, joiners and leavers, salary changes, advances and bonuses</td><td>Chase gaps and question anything unusual</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">2. Calculation</th><td>Answer queries</td><td>Work out gross pay, deductions and net pay</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">3. Approval</th><td>Review the summary and approve it</td><td>Show changes from last month</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">4. Payment</th><td>Pay salaries from your own account</td><td>Provide the payment file, if agreed</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">5. Payslips</th><td>Decide how staff receive them</td><td>Generate payslips</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">6. Statutory</th><td>Deposit deductions, or approve deposit</td><td>Prepare TDS and, where applicable, PF and ESI details</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">7. Records</th><td>Keep the master records</td><td>Hand over monthly reports</td></tr>
        </tbody>
