<section class="section section--tint" aria-labelledby="codes-title">
  <div class="wrap two-col">
    <div>
      <h2 id="codes-title">The labour codes: why to ask now</h2>
      <p>Secondary sources report that India's four labour codes came into force on 21 November 2025. Among other things, they use a common definition of wages, in which certain excluded allowances above a limit (commonly described as 50% of total pay) are treated as wages.</p>
      <p class="para">This may affect how salaries are structured, and what is calculated on them. Sources differ on how far this has taken effect for PF, and on the state of the final rules, so we have not stated a rule here.</p>
      <p class="para"><strong>What to do:</strong> ask your provider or a labour law professional whether your salary structure has been reviewed against the codes.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h2>Does PF or ESI apply to you?</h2>
      <p>It depends on factors such as your establishment and headcount and, for ESI, the employee's wages. A wage ceiling of ₹21,000 is widely cited for ESI, but confirm this and the rules for your business with {% ext "https://www.epfindia.gov.in/", "EPFO" %} and {% ext "https://www.esic.gov.in/", "ESIC" %}.</p>
      <p class="para">Do not assume you are exempt because you are small. Do not assume the rules for your previous employer apply to you either.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section" aria-labelledby="ask-title">
  <div class="wrap layout-side">
    <div class="prose">
      <h2 id="ask-title" class="first-h2">Questions to ask a provider</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>What is your cut-off date for inputs, and what if I am late?</li>
        <li>Will you show me each employee's change from last month?</li>
        <li>Who handles TDS on salaries, and who issues the annual certificate?</li>
        <li>Are PF and ESI registration and returns included, or only calculation?</li>
        <li>Who checks new hires' PF and ESI details?</li>
        <li>How do you handle final settlements for those leaving?</li>
        <li>How is salary data kept confidential, and who can see it?</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 id="mistakes">Common mistakes</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Attendance in one place and advances in another,</strong> so deductions are missed.</li>
        <li><strong>Paying cash with no record,</strong> which leaves you without proof.</li>
        <li><strong>Treating everyone as a contractor</strong> to avoid payroll. The label does not decide what the relationship is, so ask for advice if you are unsure.</li>
        <li><strong>Sharing a full salary sheet by group chat.</strong> Salary data deserves care.</li>
        <li><strong>Not collecting employee tax declarations,</strong> which leads to wrong TDS.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 id="fees">What affects the fee</h2>
      <p>Number of employees, variable pay, attendance complexity, number of locations, statutory filings included, and whether final settlements are covered. AccountOrbit does not set fees.</p>

      <h2 id="link">Related work</h2>
